THE ONE-SENTENCE DEFINITION
Smart Notes + Receipts is the Naya Power law that turns meaningful human intelligence into persistent, structured, reusable knowledge — and provides verifiable evidence when that intelligence has actually been captured.
This is more than taking notes.
It is the beginning of a system in which:
Experience becomes memory.
Memory becomes knowledge.
Knowledge becomes intelligence.
Intelligence improves action.
Action creates new experience.
And the cycle compounds.

THE CORE PROMISE
When something matters, you should not have to trust that Naya said she remembered it.
You should be able to know:
It was captured.
And when something has been captured, you should be able to know:
What was captured.
When it was captured.
What it came from.
Where it lives.
What it is connected to.
Whether it was verified.
Whether it is private or shared.
That is the purpose of the Receipt.

01 — WHY THIS LAW EXISTS
Human beings generate valuable intelligence constantly.
We experience:
ideas;
discoveries;
decisions;
insights;
breakthroughs;
mistakes;
lessons;
successes;
failures;
questions;
opportunities;
problems;
solutions;
goals;
commitments;
observations;
relationships;
project developments;
creative concepts;
personal realizations.
But most of that intelligence is temporary.
A thought occurs.
A breakthrough happens.
A decision is made.
A problem is solved.
A lesson is learned.
Then the conversation ends.
Life continues.
And eventually someone asks:
“What was that thing we figured out?”
Too often, the answer is:
“I don't remember.”
Naya Power exists to change that.

02 — THE PROBLEM WITH ORDINARY NOTES
A conventional notes system generally asks:
“What do you want to write down?”
Naya Power asks a more important question:
“What intelligence should survive this moment so that it can make the future better?”
That is a fundamentally different idea.
A Smart Note is not simply a transcript.
It is not a screenshot.
It is not a pile of copied conversation.
It is not an arbitrary database record.
It is:
Meaningful intelligence intentionally preserved for future use.

03 — THE PROBLEM WITH ORDINARY AI MEMORY
AI systems can appear to remember.
But appearance is not proof.
There is a critical difference between:
“Naya remembers this.”
and:
“The system actually persisted this information and can prove where it is.”
Naya Power is built around that distinction.
A trustworthy intelligence system must know the difference between:
KNOWING
Information available in the current interaction.
REMEMBERING
Information available from actual persistent memory.
INFERENCING
Something Naya believes based on available information.
VERIFYING
Something supported by evidence.
These must never be falsely represented as the same thing.

04 — THE SMART NOTE PRINCIPLE
The central principle is:
When something matters, capture the intelligence — not merely the conversation surrounding it.
For example:
Conversation
“We changed the assessment opening because people were getting confused.”
A weak note might simply copy that sentence.
A Smart Note should preserve the useful intelligence:
Assessment onboarding should clearly explain the expected outcome before asking the user to begin, because ambiguity at the beginning can create unnecessary friction.
The second has future value.
That is the difference.

