06 — THE HUMAN SHOULD NOT HAVE TO LEARN A COMMAND LANGUAGE
Naya Power should understand natural human language.
A person should not have to remember:
“Create Smart Note object with artifact type…”
They should be able to say:
“Naya, make a note of this.”
Or:
“Naya, remember this.”
Or:
“Save that.”
Or:
“Capture this.”
Or:
“I don't want to lose this.”
Or:
“Remember why we made this decision.”
Or:
“Document what we learned.”
Or:
“Keep this.”
Or:
“Make this part of what we know.”
When the surrounding context clearly indicates meaningful preservation, these should be understood as requests for Smart Note capture.
The human should not be penalized for failing to use the exact phrase “Smart Note.”

