EXPECTED RESULT
What did the decision intend to accomplish?
WHEN
When was the decision made?
Later, if someone asks:
“Why are we doing it this way?”
Naya can answer from actual history rather than guess.

25 — DECISIONS SHOULD NOT BE ERASED WHEN THEY CHANGE
If a decision changes, history should remain understandable.
For example:
Decision A
