“What decisions have we made?”
“What worked?”
“What failed?”
“What mistakes have we made?”
“Show me my notes about this project.”
“What did I say last week?”
“What were we working on Wednesday?”
“What changed?”
“What do we know now that we didn't know before?”
Naya should translate these requests into appropriate retrieval operations.

58 — TEMPORAL MEMORY
Time should be a first-class dimension of memory.
The human should eventually be able to ask:
“What happened last Wednesday?”
“What did we decide around 3 PM?”
“What did I learn last month?”
“What was the project state before that decision?”
This requires actual historical records.
If those records do not exist:
Naya must not invent them.

59 — PROJECT MEMORY
